<%# Fuime: same pitch as invite.html.erb, framed as a nudge. Same token, same
    7-day clock (TEEN_GROWTH G5). Branches on merchant-of-record for the same
    reason the first email does — the signature gates payouts under MoR and
    activation under Connect. %>
<p>
  Hi —
</p>

<p>
  This is a reminder: <strong><%= @minor_name %></strong> set up
  <% if @venture_name.present? %>
    <strong><%= @venture_name %></strong>
  <% else %>
    a business
  <% end %>
  on Fuime, a financial platform for young founders, and they're still
  waiting for a parent or guardian to sign off. <%= @minor_name %> named you.
</p>

<% if @stage == :day6 %>
  <p>
    The link expires
    <strong><%= @expires_at ? l(@expires_at.to_date, format: :long) : "soon" %></strong>.
    After that, opening it will offer to send you a fresh one.
  </p>
<% end %>

<p>
  <% if @merchant_of_record %>
    <%# Not "they can sell": selling under MoR waits on Fuime's vetting
        (Fuime::OperatorEligibility), which may not have happened yet. %>
    Until you accept, they cannot get paid.
  <% else %>
    Until you accept, their business cannot go live and they cannot get paid.
  <% end %>
  Accepting makes you the legal signer and responsible adult for
  <%= @venture_name.presence || "their business" %>; <%= @minor_name %> runs
  it day to day.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>What you're agreeing to</strong> <em>(one page, about two minutes)</em>
</p>

<ul>
  <li>You're the legal signer for <%= @venture_name.presence || "their business" %>. <%= @minor_name %> runs it day to day.</li>
  <li>You can see every sale and every dollar, always. <%= @minor_name %> can't turn that off.</li>
  <% if @merchant_of_record %>
    <%# Same reasoning as invite.html.erb: the parent gates whether money can go
        out (Event#payout_setup_blockers), not each weekly Fuime::PayoutBatch. %>
    <li>Nothing is paid out until you've accepted and set up where the money goes.</li>
  <% else %>
    <li>Nothing goes live until you accept.</li>
  <% end %>
</ul>

<p>
  <%= link_to "Review and sign", @accept_url,
              style: "display:inline-block;background:#2242FF;color:#ffffff;padding:12px 20px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:8px;font-weight:600;" %>
</p>

<p style="word-break: break-all;">
  Or paste this link into your browser:<br>
  <%= link_to @accept_url, @accept_url %>
</p>

<p>
  <% if @merchant_of_record %>
    We won't ask for a Social Security number, an ID, or a payment. When
    there's money to send, we'll ask where it should go.
  <% else %>
    Accepting is free and doesn't ask for an ID. Before any money moves,
    Stripe will need identity details from the account owner.
  <% end %>
</p>

<p>
  If you already accepted, you can ignore this. Not expecting this? Ignore
  it — nothing happens unless you accept.
</p>

<p>
  Questions? Reply to this email or write to <%= @support_email %>.
</p>

<p>
  Thanks,<br>
  The Fuime team
</p>
